1. Problem Statement
   Develop a C++ program to represent hospital equipment units as vertices and possible wiring connections as weighted edges.
   Apply Kruskal's algorithm to find the minimum-cost wiring connections.
   Modify the program to update an edge weight and recalculate the minimum spanning tree, display each selected edge with its
   weight and running total cost, and detect whether the graph is disconnected and a spanning tree can be formed.

2. Solution
   The program represents hospital equipment as vertices and wiring connections as weighted edges. Kruskal's algorithm sorts the edges by weight and selects the 
   lowest-cost connections without creating cycles.
   The DSU data structure identifies cycles, while the running total records the cost after each selected edge. The program also allows the user to update an  
   existing edge weight and recalculate the minimum spanning tree. If the number of selected edges is less than V - 1, the graph is disconnected and a spanning 
   tree cannot be formed.
